00:00:05.269 --> 00:00:07.190 align:start position:0%
the european union's competitiveness  council aims this month to breathe life  into a new generation of public and  private partnerships  that will help create jobs and boost  economic growth  the partnerships will contribute to the  launch of large-scale and long-term  innovation projects  under the eu's massive new research  program horizon 2020  they'll focus on innovative medicine  more effective diagnostics and  treatments  with the aim of improving the health and  well-being of europeans  other partnerships include bio-based  industries aeronautics  electronics fuel cells and hydrogen the  european commission estimates that the  projects could draw  17 billion euros in investment in public  debate the council will seek a general  political approach  on the european program for monitoring  the earth from satellites  known as copernicus the program will be  used to support the agriculture and  fisheries sectors  and will help in disaster response work  including fighting forest fires  elsewhere on the agenda ministers will  try to reach a common position  concerning new rules on breaches of  anti-trust laws  which has happened in the car industry  among other sectors  the proposals could make it easier for  victims of cartels  to receive compensation for loss of  business and  lost profits
 

